      <TableCell><code>distinguisherMethod</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>FlowDistinguisherMethod specifies the method of a flow distinguisher.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>matchingPrecedence</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>integer</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>matchingPrecedence</code> is used to choose among the FlowSchemas that match a given request. The chosen FlowSchema is among those with the numerically lowest (which we take to be logically highest) MatchingPrecedence.  Each MatchingPrecedence value must be ranged in [1,10000]. Note that if the precedence is not specified, it will be set to 1000 as default.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>priorityLevelConfiguration</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>PriorityLevelConfigurationReference contains information that points to the "request-priority" being used.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
